# Generated by tools/review_sheet.py from FAILURES.md + BREAKAGES.md.
# A working aid for the 19 verdicts, not a deliverable — regenerate rather than commit.
deliverables/VERDICTS.md
deliverables/VERDICTS-FULL.md

# graphify — the knowledge graph of this repo (see study/README.md).
# Same rule the corpus uses: BULK OUT, RECORD IN. What the lab PC needs to
# query the graph is committed, because D29 says handoff goes through git;
# what it can rebuild in one command, or what is machine-specific, is not.
#
#   committed   graph.json          1.0M  the graph itself. Rebuilding costs
#                                         ~334k LLM tokens across 3 agents.
#               GRAPH_REPORT.md      32K  god nodes, communities, audit trail
#               manifest.json        16K  lets `--update` re-extract only what
#                                         changed; contains no absolute paths
#               .graphify_labels.json 4K  the 68 community names, hand-written
#
#   ignored     graph.html          920K  one command from graph.json
#               cache/              1.2M  regenerable, and re-derived per machine
#               .graphify_python           an ABSOLUTE path to a Mac uv venv —
#               .graphify_root             committing these would break the lab PC
#               cost.json                  local token accounting
graphify-out/graph.html
graphify-out/cache/
graphify-out/.graphify_python
graphify-out/.graphify_root
graphify-out/cost.json
